From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 08:25:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pm_shim: find the SEP power state through
 the sleep node

The enclave's sleep request is meant to go out at the sleep driver's last
refusal, so that a sleep refused anywhere before it never finds the
enclave told: a gated enclave comes back only through a real sleep. The
commit step needs the enclave's power state word, which it looks up
through the SEP node's power-domains. The T8132 device trees keep the SEP
domain out of genpd, so that node lists none, the lookup fails with
-ENOENT, and the request is sent at .suspend instead. Waking the enclave
after a sleep cannot clear its DEV_DISABLE bit for the same reason.

On the J604 an early request turns every suspend-to-RAM that does not
reach the final power-down (pm_test "devices", any later refusal) into a
reset of the machine about 45 s after the resume. Without the request
(apple_sep.debug_skip_sleep_request) the same runs survive; leaving out
the ANS sleep stop instead does not help.

Fall back to the domain the sleep driver's node names in
apple,sep-domain, which that driver already reads for the same state word
before it powers the SoC down. Nodes that list power-domains are not
affected.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pm_shim.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pm_shim.c b/drivers/soc/apple/pm_shim.c
index f670028033..0d1508ad77 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pm_shim.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pm_shim.c
@@ -68,13 +68,36 @@ static struct notifier_block sep_pm_nb = {
 	.notifier_call = sep_pm_notify,
 };
 
-/* The enclave's own domain is the first one its node lists. */
+/*
+ * The enclave's own domain, with a reference held: the first one its node
+ * lists or, where the node lists none (T8132 keeps the SEP domain out of
+ * genpd), the one the sleep driver's node names in apple,sep-domain, which
+ * that driver already reads for the same state word.
+ */
+static struct device_node *sep_pm_domain_node(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct device_node *np, *sleep;
+
+	np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "power-domains", 0);
+	if (np)
+		return np;
+
+	sleep = of_find_node_with_property(NULL, "apple,sep-domain");
+	if (!sleep)
+		return NULL;
+	if (of_device_is_available(sleep))
+		np = of_parse_phandle(sleep, "apple,sep-domain", 0);
+	of_node_put(sleep);
+
+	return np;
+}
+
 static int sep_pm_domain(struct device *dev, struct regmap **regmap, u32 *offset)
 {
 	struct device_node *np;
 	int ret;
 
-	np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "power-domains", 0);
+	np = sep_pm_domain_node(dev);
 	if (!np)
 		return -ENOENT;
 
@@ -288,7 +311,7 @@ int sep_pm_commit_prepare(void *ptr, void *mbox, u64 msg0, u32 msg1, u64 reply,
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	if (c->registered)
 		return -EBUSY;
-	np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "power-domains", 0);
+	np = sep_pm_domain_node(dev);
 	if (!np)
 		return -ENOENT;
 	ret = of_property_read_u32(np, "reg", &offset);
